Hitchhiking is not an offence in Austrian law; where you stand is. [https://www.ris.bka.gv.at/NormDokument.wxe?Abfrage=Bundesnormen&Gesetzesnummer=10011336&Paragraf=46 § 46(1) of the ''Straßenverkehrsordnung 1960''] reserves the ''Autobahn'' for motor vehicles built for more than 60 km/h and states that all other traffic, "in particular pedestrian traffic", is forbidden on it — carriageway, ''Pannenstreifen'' and on-ramp alike. The same paragraph makes one narrow exception for going in on foot: at a border crossing or a toll station you may enter the Autobahn for business connected with the crossing. § 46(4)(e) allows vehicles to stop or park only at the places marked by signs, meaning the ''Rastplätze'' and ''Raststationen'' — which is exactly where you ask drivers for the next ride. On ''Bundesstraßen'' and everything smaller hitchhiking is unregulated and legal, so thumb before the motorway sign.
